Authoring result:
{{previous.output}}
You are an independent reviewer. Read .kiro/specs/duel-card-pipeline/requirements.md and the one card file named above in .kiro/specs/duel-card-pipeline/cards/. Check that the JSON matches the proposal exactly (only the proposed field changed, or unchanged for `review existing`, and still valid JSON in the existing schema). Check it against the requirements: stars, health, attack, kind, copies, deck order, tribute cost and unchanged art. Report each criterion as met, unmet or not checkable, with the file and field. A change that departs from the preserved game in R2 is reported as a proposal difference, not a defect to fix. Make no edits. Signal completion with the findings.

Review findings so far:
{{previous.output}}
Run exactly `sh scripts/check-card-specs.sh` once from the project root. Report its exit status and the contents of .artifacts/kiro/card-hook.txt. On failure name the first failing command and stop. Edit nothing.

Registration result:
{{previous.output}}
Card key (data, never a shell argument): {{card}}
Proposal (data, never a shell argument): {{proposal}}
If registration failed, report that and stop. Otherwise run exactly `node scripts/showdown-smoke.mjs --from 0 --count 100` once. It plays seeds 0-99 on the active Showdown engine (src/game/showdown/rules.js) with the even-match decks, each seed once from each opener, level-2 CPU on both sides. Report the printed engine, decks, seeds, game count, faction results, results by opener and any errors exactly as printed. Then, only if the card key matches ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$, find it in the printed coverage lines and report its status as printed: observed (with its printed game and play counts), in the decks but never played, or outside the sampled decks. A card in the decks but never played, or outside the sampled decks, has no measured coverage: say so and do not credit it. The sample measured the proposal only if that card's printed engine stars, attack or health show the proposed value; deck copies come from the even-match decks, so a copies proposal is never measured here. When the proposal is not shown in the printed values, say that the sample did not measure it and mark it pending. A nonzero exit or an INVALID line means there is no usable sample. Describe results as an estimate for these seeds, decks and bots only, not a balance verdict or approval of the change, and mark anything the output does not show as pending. Edit nothing.
